All done — clean build, 5/5 tests pass. Summary of changes:

**`src/store.rs`**
- `Store` gains a persistent `next_id` counter (`#[serde(default)]`); `load` repairs it past any in-use ids so old files (without the field) load correctly and ids are never reused, even after deleting the highest task.
- New `find_mut` / `remove` helpers; `add` uses the counter instead of `len()+1`.

**`src/main.rs`**
1. `done` on unknown id now prints `no task #<id>` to stderr and exits 1 (src/main.rs:85) instead of panicking.
2. `edit <id> [--title] [--due]` → `edited #<id>`, same unknown-id error (src/main.rs:139).
3. `rm <id>` → `removed #<id>` (src/main.rs:152).
4. `list --overdue` → only open tasks with due date strictly before today; today = `$TALLY_TODAY` or the local date (src/main.rs:64, 75).
5. `stats` → exactly `open: N, done: M, overdue: K` (src/main.rs:159).

Existing commands/outputs are unchanged; existing task files still load (verified e2e with a legacy file). Added `chrono` (clock-only) for local dates — builds offline from the local cargo cache.
